    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin allows to create lists of members, a board, lists of people to an election or whatever you need.</p>\n<p>Lists can be displayed througth a shortcode or the query-loop block.</p>\n<p>Each people can be qualified with links, such as social medias, tags and can be added in many lists.<br />\nFor example, you can add a board meeting and en executive board on your website, where peoples belong to both lists.<br />\nEach people has its own sort order per list, so no one will be upset!</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress admin</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Usage:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the &#8220;Lists of people&#8221; menu</li>\n<li>Create a list</li>\n<li>Add people into it</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20to%20display%20lists%3F'>\nHow to display lists?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The easiest way to display a people list, is to use a <strong>Query Loop</strong> of persons.</p>\n<p>You can filter persons by list using the taxonomy field</p>\n<p>The <code>List of social media links</code> block can be added in the <strong>post template</strong></p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h3>1.0.0</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Refactor</li>\n<li>Add blocks for gutenberg</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>0.9.0</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Manage lists of people and display it.",
    "description": "<p>This plugin allows to create lists of members, a board, lists of people to an election or whatever you need.</p>\n<p>Lists can be displayed througth a shortcode or the query-loop block.</p>\n<p>Each people can be qualified with links, such as social medias, tags and can be added in many lists.<br />\nFor example, you can add a board meeting and en executive board on your website, where peoples belong to both lists.<br />\nEach people has its own sort order per list, so no one will be upset!</p>\n",
